Subject: [PATCH 04043/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1 (ARC
 NORTH STAR; PRIMARY; HEADLINE) -- REPLACE THE 0.12-ACCURATE FREE-FORM ENGINE
 WITH THE EXISTING STRUCTURED ProductWorldModel. The 2026-06-25 end-to-end
 measurement proved the free-form LLM engine induction is the binding wall:
 lp85's L1 world model reproduced only 0.12 of observed transitions
 (world_model_accuracy_below_threshold) -- the model writes a placeholder
 engine. A structured engine with the EXACT (grid,action,data)->next_grid
 signature ALREADY EXISTS (ProductWorldModel.engine,
 arc_executable_world_model.py:427) fed by induce_programmatic_object_experts
 (:331). Build a load_engine adapter that returns (ProductWorldModel(induced
 experts).engine, goal) and wire it (env-gated CARNOT_ARC_STRUCTURED_ENGINE=1)
 into the live level_up_reinduction call site (arc_competition_agent.py:2494,
 in place of e3.load_engine). NON-DEGENERACY GATE INLINE: PROVE the structured
 engine actually changes cells (engine output differs from the input grid on
 >0 actions) BEFORE any accuracy claim. WIN: the structured engine's held-out
 transition accuracy on >=1 real game (lp85/sc25/m0r0) beats the free-form
 0.12 by a wide margin (target >=0.5) AND the L2 reinduction runs on it
 without proposer_failed OR a multi-level probe reaches L2 offline-reproduced.
 verifier_is_oracle:false. live_agent_self_discovery. retire_if_same_verdict.

